parts.output:
### Configure Plugin Lazy Loading with Multiple Triggers

Source: https://github.com/nix-community/nixvim/blob/main/docs/user-guide/lazy-loading.md

Enable lazy loading for a plugin and specify multiple trigger conditions, such as a command and a set of keymaps. Ensure the plugin is enabled.

```nix
{
  plugins.toggleterm = {
    enable = true;
    lazyLoad.settings = {
      cmd = "ToggleTerm";
      keys = [
        "<leader>tg"
        "<leader>gg"
      ];
    };
  };
}
```

--------------------------------

### Register and Configure Extra Nixvim Plugins

Source: https://github.com/nix-community/nixvim/blob/main/docs/user-guide/faq.md

Use `extraPlugins` to register plugins packaged in nixpkgs and `extraConfigLua` to configure them.

```nix
extraPlugins = [pkgs.vimPlugins."<plugin name>"]
extraConfigLua = "require('my-plugin').setup({foo = \"bar\"})";
```

--------------------------------

### Enable a Nixvim plugin

Source: https://github.com/nix-community/nixvim/blob/main/README.md

Enable a supported plugin by setting its module enable option to true.

```nix
{
  programs.nixvim = {
    plugins.lightline.enable = true;
  };
}
```

### Lazy Loading > Enabling Lazy Loading Per Plugin

Source: https://github.com/nix-community/nixvim/blob/main/docs/user-guide/lazy-loading.md

Plugins can be configured for lazy loading by passing settings to the lazyLoad.settings option. By default, Nixvim automatically generates the necessary setup code to trigger the plugin when specified conditions are met. Users can explicitly disable lazy loading for a plugin by setting lazyLoad.enable to false.

--------------------------------

### Nixvim > How does it work? > Plugin settings

Source: https://github.com/nix-community/nixvim/blob/main/README.md

Most plugins include a settings option that accepts Nix attribute sets, which are translated into Lua tables and passed to the plugin's setup function. This allows users to configure plugin options even when explicit Nix options are not provided.
<dcp-message-id>m0078</dcp-message-id>

### Configure Neovim Options

Source: https://github.com/nix-community/nixvim/blob/main/README.md

Set Neovim configuration options by defining the opts attribute in your Nixvim configuration.

```nix
{
  programs.nixvim = {
    opts = {
      number = true;         # Show line numbers
      relativenumber = true; # Show relative line numbers

      shiftwidth = 2;        # Tab width should be 2
    };
  };
}
```

### Custom LSP server modules

Source: https://github.com/nix-community/nixvim/blob/main/modules/lsp/servers/custom/README.md

Modules related to specific LSP servers are located in this directory. Files are automatically imported into their respective submodules based on their filename. For instance, `foo.nix` or `foo/default.nix` would be imported into the `lsp.servers.foo` submodule. A corresponding `lsp.servers.<name>` option must be defined for each module in this directory.
<dcp-message-id>m0078</dcp-message-id>

### Complete real-world cmp + luasnip integration

Source: https://github.com/nix-community/nixvim/blob/main/tests/test-sources/example-configurations/issues.nix

Full configuration combining snippet expansion, luasnip as a source, and source-specific options like show_autosnippets.

```nix
cmp = {
        enable = true;
        autoEnableSources = true;

        settings = {
          formatting = {
            format = ''
              require("lspkind").cmp_format({
                      mode="symbol",
                      maxwidth = 50,
                      ellipsis_char = "..."
              })
            '';
          };

          snippet = {
            expand = ''
              function(args)
                require("luasnip").lsp_expand(args.body)
              end
            '';
          };
          sources = [
            { name = "nvim_lsp"; }
            {
              name = "luasnip";
              option = {
                show_autosnippets = true;
              };
            }
            { name = "path"; }
            { name = "buffer"; }
          ];
        };
      };
```
<dcp-message-id>m0078</dcp-message-id>

