You are asking how to configure `cmp` settings, specifically `cmp.mapping.preset.insert`, within Nixvim. In Nixvim, `cmp` mappings are configured within the `plugins.cmp.settings.mapping` option. To use `cmp.mapping.preset.insert` or any other raw Lua code, you need to use Nixvim's `__raw` attribute.  

## Configuring `cmp` Mappings

The `cmp` plugin in Nixvim exposes a `settings.mapping` option for defining keybindings.  This option expects an attribute set where keys are the Neovim keybindings and values are the corresponding Lua actions. 

### Using `__raw` for `cmp.mapping.preset.insert`

When you need to provide a literal Lua snippet, such as `cmp.mapping.preset.insert`, you must use the `__raw` attribute.  This tells Nixvim to treat the value as raw Lua code rather than attempting to serialize it as a Nix data structure. 

Here's the correct Nix syntax for configuring `cmp.mapping.preset.insert` within your Nixvim configuration:

```nix
{
  plugins.cmp = {
    enable = true;
    settings = {
      mapping.__raw = ''
        cmp.mapping.preset.insert({
          ['<C-b>'] = cmp.mapping.scroll_docs(-4),
          ['<C-f>'] = cmp.mapping.scroll_docs(4),
          ['<C-Space>'] = cmp.mapping.complete(),
          ['<C-e>'] = cmp.mapping.abort(),
          ['<CR>'] = cmp.mapping.confirm({ select = true }),
        })
      '';
    };
  };
}
```  

This example demonstrates how to set up common keybindings using `cmp.mapping.preset.insert` by assigning the entire Lua function call as a raw string to `mapping.__raw`. 

## How it Works

The `plugins.cmp` module in Nixvim uses `lib.nixvim.plugins.mkNeovimPlugin` to define the `cmp` plugin.  The `settings` attribute you define in your Nix configuration is passed to the `cmp.setup()` Lua function.  When Nixvim encounters an attribute with `__raw`, it directly inserts the string value into the generated Lua configuration without further processing. 

## Notes

The `plugins.cmp.options.settings-options.nix` file defines the available options for the `cmp` plugin, including the `mapping` option.  The `plugins.cmp.options.default.nix` file provides an example of how to use `mapping.__raw` with `cmp.mapping.preset.insert`.  Similarly, `tests/test-sources/plugins/cmp/default.nix` also contains an example of this configuration. 

